NPC: net_seller
LOCATION: quay_market
SCHEDULE: morning=quay_market, midday=quay_market, evening=closed, night=closed

TOPIC: default
  GATE: always
  TAG: net_seller_default
  TIME: 2
  NET SELLER: "Nets, lines, or crabbing pots. Otherwise you're in my light."

TOPIC: crew_omission
  GATE: topic_done(local_historian, crew_omission_official) AND NOT topic_done(net_seller, crew_omission)
  TAG: net_seller_crew_omission
  LABEL: "Ask why the town's history leaves out the crew's names"
  TIME: 4
  WALTER CORWIN: "The men who drowned in 1823 — their names aren't in any record."
  NET SELLER: "Ours are."
  WALTER CORWIN: "Where?"
  NET SELLER: "In the families. In the boats we named after them.\nIn the berths we don't give to strangers."
  [She does not look up from the netting needle.]
  NET SELLER: "You're asking why the town didn't write them down.\nThe town didn't lose them.\nWe did."
  NOTEBOOK: net_seller_crew_omission | "The net seller said the drowned crew's names are preserved in the harbor families, not in civic records. She drew a clear line between 'the town' and 'we.'"